Changes on the official distribution to compile version 2.1.11 in windows:

1) In lis.h 
   LIS_DEBUG_FUNC_IN and LIS_DEBUG_FUNC_OUT changed to avoid printing messages
   in debug mode

2) The original Windows configuration script assumes that if you request MPI 
   support, that implies using the Intel compiler. That is not our environment 
   though. The win\configure.bat file was updated to include a new --enable-impimsvc 
   option that sets the impi variable to 1 but keeps intelc as 0. 
   The win\Makefile.in file was also updated to include the correct directives
   for using the MPI library with MSVC.
   To highlight the changes, the original version 2.1.11 files were commited
   and (revision 5118) then the changed files were commited again (revision 5119).

3) In lis.h and src/solver
   Add a new stop criterion: maximum iterations without improvement (-maxiter_noimp, default = 100) 
   With this addition, the solver can stop early and save computational time when detecting 
   that the iterations are not improving the residual. It is especially useful for difficult 
   matrices, where methods can get stuck on a plateau or diverge with inf/nan. 
   Setting `-maxiter_noimp 0`  disables this feature. For now, it is only available for 
   double precision.


4) Windows ONLY - NOT a distribution change:
   LIS depends on "Win32.Mak" originally found on the Windows 7.1A SDK. 
   It contains several definitions that are used by the LIS makefile. 

   On MSVC 2022 it could be installed by the optional package 
   "C++ Windows XP support for VS 2017 (v141)", and would be installed on 
   "C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft SDKs\Windows\v7.1A\Include\Win32.Mak".

   Unfortunatelly, newer versions of MSVC2026 don't include that package anymore, 
   so one needs to manually download/setup the file where LIS can find it.

